th me  research also shows that on a scale of  choosing people and friends and family  that mostly disagree with you from  choosing friends and family that mostly  agree with you the average American will  choose people  they generally agree with on politics  also when there's groups of people that  generally agree with each other  statistics have shown that 79 percent of  them are likely to talk about politics  but if there's groups of people that  disagree on politics and only 29 percent  of them will actually talk about  politics so the problem with this is  then we're creating these silos of  opinions and then the silo these  opinions end up becoming a little bit  more extreme than they should be  other studies have shown that when  people with different perspectives come  together they end up forming the  consensus but when there's groups of  people that are like-minded made up of  like-minded individuals they will tend  to form a consensus that is much more  extreme so this imprint of a story from  when I was in elementary school my  favorite band was New Kids on the Block  yeah the problem is I had never heard a  New Kids on the Block song before my  life so that was purely a decision of  consensus and not an informed decision  so where does that bring us here today  well basically if we want to be the most  informed as we can be on the issues then  we need to talk more with people that we  disagree with if we can talk more with  people that we disagree with maybe we  can move this average arrow more towards  the neutral center where people  generally just naturally choose to talk  to people they agree with and disagree  with if we can talk to people on both  sides of the or if we can understand  both sides of the stories then we will  become more understanding will  stereotype less and we will be more  informed if we understand both sides of  the story then we will learn to  appreciate differing opinions and by  talking more we can actually understand  each other and empathize more with each  other and build relationships better  and then in the end we don't have to be  so scared to talk about politics we  don't have to worry about politics  coming in between our relationships so I  challenge you all to go find some  friends and family at least half of  which you disagree with in politics go  take them out to coffee or get a lunch  with them and find out what it is that  they believe don't just hear what they  have to say but truly listen and truly  understand why why it is that they  believe what they believe not only will  you learn from this but I strongly  believe that you will also find out that  you have more in common than you thought  so go challenge yourself to become more  informed politically thank you very much  you
 

